  "structural_phenomena": [
    {
      "id": "PHENOMENON_01_UNUSED_HEADLINE_ISMODULAR_AND_INTERNAL_LEVEL_LOWERING_CONTRADICTION",
      "files": [
        "P2M/Sol/S_FreyPackage_no_frey_package.lean:139-142",
        "P2M/Sol/S_FreyPackage_level_lowering_to_two.lean:129-134",
        "P2M/Sol/S_FreyPackage_level_lowering_to_two_of_conductorLevel.lean:163-170",
        "Definitions/Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity.lean:98-102"
      ],
      "verified_fact": "In S_FreyPackage_level_lowering_to_two.lean (lines 129-134), the explicit hypothesis (hmod : P.freyCurve.IsModular) passed from frey_isModular is silenced by `set_option linter.unusedVariables false in` and not consumed; instead, the proof invokes `P.modularRepOfConductorLevel` (which separately retains `P.IsConductorLevel N`). Furthermore, in S_FreyPackage_level_lowering_to_two_of_conductorLevel.lean (lines 163-170), level lowering lowers N to M | 2 (M in {1, 2}), applies S2_Gamma0_eq_zero_of_dvd_two inside the lemma to derive a contradiction with hf.ne_zero, and uses `absurd` to return `exists f : CuspForm (Gamma0 2) 2, f != 0`."
    },
    {
      "id": "PHENOMENON_02_COUNTERFACTUAL_CARRIER_BUNDLING_AND_SMALL_PRIME_EX_FALSO_DISCHARGE",
      "files": [
        "Definitions/Def_FLTPrelim_FreyPackage.lean:12-34",
        "P2M/Sol/S_FreyPackage_frey_no_cofixed_eleven.lean:14-24",
        "P2M/Sol/S_FreyPackage_frey_no_cofixed_small.lean:16-29",
        "P2M/Sol/S_FreyPackage_Mazur_Frey.lean:68-91"
      ],
      "verified_fact": "`FreyPackage` bundles the counterfactual equality `hFLT : a^p + b^p = c^p` directly into the carrier type. In `S_FreyPackage_frey_no_cofixed_eleven.lean` (lines 14-24) and `S_FreyPackage_frey_no_cofixed_small.lean` (lines 16-29), the absence of a Galois-stable cofixed line (`not HasGaloisStableCofixedLine`, where the 1-dimensional quotient has trivial G_Q-action) for p in {5, 7, 11, 13} is discharged not by modular curve isogeny analysis, but by importing standalone classical proofs `fermatLastTheoremEleven/Five/Seven/Thirteen`, deducing `P.p != p_0` from `P.hFLT`, and applying `absurd hp`."
    },
    {
      "id": "PHENOMENON_03_MODEL_DEPENDENT_INTEGRAL_WEIERSTRASS_PREDICATE",
      "files": [
        "Definitions/Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity.lean:82-97",
        "Definitions/Def_FLTPrelim_ModularRep.lean:31-88",
        "Definitions/Def_WeierstrassCurve_Mlc1RowStatement.lean:9-19"
      ],
      "verified_fact": "`IsGoodPrimeFor` and `IsSemistableModel` are defined directly on an integral equation `W : WeierstrassCurve Z` via `not (p | W.Delta)` and `(p | W.Delta -> not (p | W.c4))` without a global minimal model condition. Under an isomorphic coordinate scaling `(x,y) -> (u^2 x, u^3 y)` (such as u = 2 on E_11), `Delta` scales by `u^12` and `c4` by `u^4`, so `2 | Delta'` and `2 | c4'`, falsifying the raw equation predicate `IsSemistableModel` on the scaled model."
    }
  ],
